#!/bin/bash
# Restart WirePlumber after resume.
#
# liquidark's xHCI controllers do not survive suspend — every resume logs
# "xHC error in resume, USBSTS 0x401, Reinit" and "root hub lost power or was
# reset". The USB audio cards themselves come back fine (the kernel resets them
# in place; there is no disconnect and no re-enumeration), but WirePlumber's
# graph does not always: on 2026-09-03 the S/PDIF sink node was caught mixing
# near-silence while every reading — links, volumes, mixer, USB endpoint —
# looked healthy. Reopening the PCM did not clear it; only destroying and
# recreating the node, which restarting WirePlumber does, brought it back.
#
# An earlier attempt parked each card's profile at "off" before sleep to close
# the PCM cleanly. It could not work from hypridle's before_sleep_cmd: hypridle
# releases its sleep inhibitor when the *lock* completes, not when the command
# finishes, so the teardown had ~400ms before the kernel froze it mid-flight.
# Restarting on the way out has no such race.
#
# 2026-10-04: this script used to verify the restart by playing a 19kHz probe
# into the sink and measuring the monitor, retrying up to three times. It was
# removed because it did not work: from 09-04 to 10-04 it reported "still
# silent" on 76 of 79 wakes while audio was fine (pw-record --target does not
# reliably attach to the named sink, and music playing at the time swamps the
# control band). It also cannot see the other resume failure — the S/PDIF link
# to the Scarlett / WiiM going dead downstream of a perfectly healthy sink —
# which no amount of restarting fixes. One restart, then get out of the way.
#
# Usage: audio-resume   (from after_sleep_cmd)

set -u

readonly SETTLE=3   # seconds: let the in-place USB reset finish first

sleep "$SETTLE"
systemctl --user restart wireplumber
